# Cursor Rules - Portfolio Project

## Language Requirements

**CRITICAL: All code must be written in English**

- All comments must be in English
- All variable names must be in English
- All function names must be in English
- All component names must be in English
- All file names must be in English (except for configuration files)
- All string literals displayed to users can be in any language, but code-related strings should be in English
- All documentation strings (JSDoc, docstrings) must be in English

## Code Style Guidelines

- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Write clear, concise comments explaining the "why" not the "what"
- Follow React/Next.js best practices
- Use TypeScript types for all props and state
- Prefer functional components with hooks
- Use meaningful component and file names

## Project-Specific Rules

- This is a Next.js 16 project with App Router
- Uses Tailwind CSS v4 for styling
- Uses Ant Design v6.2.0 for UI components
- Uses TypeScript for type safety
- Uses Yarn as the package manager

## When Writing Code

1. Always write code in English
2. Always write comments in English
3. Always use English for variable/function/component names
4. User-facing text (UI labels, messages) can be in any language as needed
5. Error messages and console logs should be in English for debugging purposes

